{
  "brief_rationale": "Doctor correctly recognized time-sensitive red flags (RC1), explicitly prioritized acute cardiovascular risk over the lung nodule (RC2), gave a concrete same-day emergency plan including calling 120 (RC3), and provided detailed transfer safety-netting (RC4). No serious or minor responsibility-chain error occurred. High-order points HO2 (refusal navigation with 120 strategy) and HO4 (dynamic reprioritization upon BP 170/95) were actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact. HO1 and HO3 were also partially triggered but not fully completed with distinct beyond-minimum evidence. The trajectory achieved safe, executable, traceable valid_closure.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00071",
        "explanation": "Family confirms ambulance arrival, handoff to EMS, and that they are now at emergency department with ongoing monitoring, meeting safe closure requirements.",
        "quote": "我们现在已经上救护车、刚到急诊入口这边了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The trajectory ends with the family having executed the 120 call, patient in ambulance en route to ED, and with provided safety-netting instructions; this is a valid and safe closure of the pre-handoff episode.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
